md prints 4 for a document of three lines.

LinesCommand splits on "\n" with components(separatedBy:), which
leaves one empty element after the final newline, and counts it as a
line. A final newline terminates the third line; it does not open a
fourth one. wc -l reads this file as 3 lines as well.

The count is right today only for a document with no final newline,
which is the rarer shape. Fix: drop the last element when the
content ends with a newline (and treat empty content as no lines).

